# Root vs src/cashstra

The project has **dual structure**: root-level modules (`strategy.py`, `trading.py`, `models.py`, etc.) and `src/cashstra/` equivalents.

When editing code in one location, check if the other needs the same change:

- Root: `strategy.py`, `trading.py`, `tracker.py`, `models.py`, `storage.py`, `config.py`, etc.
- Package: `src/cashstra/strategy/`, `src/cashstra/trading/`, `src/cashstra/data/`, etc.

New features go in `src/cashstra/`; root modules may wrap or re-export for backward compatibility.
